the q7 t is infinities flagship sedan  infiniti is the top range arm of  Japanese automakers Nissa the q7 t first  went on sale in germany in 2010 with its  economical 4-cylinder diesel engine this  sedan has got its sights set on the  German business class so how does the  Japanese premium sedan perform we're  going to find out car tester on the Left  stack says the Infiniti q70 is great for  long distances the double-glazing  greatly reduces exterior noise the 2.2  liter diesel engine is quiet - except  when the engine is still cold Ronnie  says that for the first few kilometers  you hear a deep humming noise but it's  not dramatic our test car has a 2.2  liter diesel engine this is the bottom  of the range engine for 4 cylinders  previously the q70 was only available  with a v6 diesel engine the common-rail  four-cylinder engine is considerably  more economical and harmonizes well with  the standard automatic transmission  though the transmission doesn't always  manage to change gears smoothly Ronnie  says that under the hood the Infiniti  q70 is a real money saver that's down to  the fact that this 2.2 liter diesel  engine is made by Daimler it was  incorporated into his vehicle especially  for the European market but with the  vehicle weighing around two tons he says  this 125 kilowatt and [ __ ] feels  slightly underpowered the Infiniti q70  excels with its distinct design thanks  to a bigger radiator grille and  redesigned headlights the q70 cuts an  even more imposing figure than before  its roofline resembles a coupe a and at  the back it ends with an overhang over  the trunk overall it has sleek rounded  lines  and the car's interior Infiniti pulls  out all the stops and a bid to live up  to its upscale image it takes a bit of  time to get used to the host of buttons  with tiny inscriptions on the steering  wheel and dashboard fewer switches would  be preferable but the sumptuous bucket  seats and the heated steering wheel are  a real joy  our car tester says he first checks out  the sound system when buying a new car  the Infiniti q70 has a Bose sound system  a good thing in itself is Ronnie but  more unusually the speakers are built  into the seats the result he feels as if  he's in a concert hall thanks to the  partnership with Daimler and the related  downsizing this diesel model of the q70  can now be bought for eight thousand  euros less than its predecessor in  Germany the sedans list price is  forty-four thousand five hundred euros  that's about how much you pay for the  basic version of the Mercedes e-class  which has an identical engine but you'll  get more fixtures and fittings with the  Infiniti many features that you usually  have to pay extra for like LED and  adaptive headlights come as standard  you
 

